{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":1,"id":"annotations","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Annotations"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Annotations add application classes and data to lines or exact source ranges without changing the token stream."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"line-decorations","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Line decorations"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Line numbers are one-based:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const result = highlighter.highlight(code, {\n  lang: 'ts',\n  decorations: [\n    { lines: 2, className: 'is-focused' },\n    { lines: [4, 6], className: 'is-highlighted' },\n  ],\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"lines: [4, 6]"},{"type":"text","value":" includes lines 4, 5, and 6."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Line decorations activate "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"th-line"},{"type":"text","value":" wrappers even when "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"lineNumbers"},{"type":"text","value":" is false."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"character-range-decorations","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Character-range decorations"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Character ranges are zero-based, end-exclusive UTF-16 offsets, matching "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"String.prototype.slice()"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const code = `const answer = unknownValue`\nconst start = code.indexOf('unknownValue')\n\nconst result = highlighter.highlight(code, {\n  lang: 'ts',\n  decorations: [\n    {\n      range: [start, start + 'unknownValue'.length],\n      className: 'is-error',\n      data: { message: 'Unknown identifier', severity: 2 },\n    },\n  ],\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The renderer splits token boundaries as needed and wraps the selected text with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"th-decoration"},{"type":"text","value":" plus your classes. Overlapping decorations remain valid nested HTML."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"line-numbers","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Line numbers"}]},{"type":"code","value":"highlighter.highlight(code, {\n  lang: 'ts',\n  lineNumbers: true,\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This adds "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"th-code--line-numbers"},{"type":"text","value":", line wrappers, and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"data-line"},{"type":"text","value":". Base theme CSS renders the number with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"::before"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"try-annotations","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Try annotations"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The rendered block combines line numbers, a focused line, and an exact character-range diagnostic."}]},{"type":"component","name":"live-example","tagName":"md-live-example","attributes":{"id":"highlight-annotations-1"},"properties":{"data-example-group":"highlight-annotations","data-collapsed-indexes":"[]","data-workspace":"{\"version\":1,\"entry\":\"/src/main.ts\",\"environment\":\"client\",\"files\":{\"/src/main.ts\":\"import { createHighlighter } from '@tanstack/highlight/core'\\nimport { ts } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/ts'\\nimport { createThemeCss } from '@tanstack/highlight/theme'\\nimport { githubDarkTheme } from '@tanstack/highlight/themes/github-dark'\\nimport { githubLightTheme } from '@tanstack/highlight/themes/github-light'\\n\\nconst source = [\\n  'type User = { name: string }',\\n  'const user = missingUser',\\n  'console.log(user.name)',\\n].join('\\\\n')\\nconst identifier = 'missingUser'\\nconst start = source.indexOf(identifier)\\n\\nconst highlighter = createHighlighter({ languages: [ts] })\\nconst result = highlighter.highlight(source, {\\n  lang: 'ts',\\n  lineNumbers: true,\\n  decorations: [\\n    { lines: 3, className: 'is-focused' },\\n    {\\n      range: [start, start + identifier.length],\\n      className: 'is-error',\\n      data: { message: 'Unknown identifier' },\\n    },\\n  ],\\n})\\n\\nconst themeCss = createThemeCss({\\n  light: githubLightTheme,\\n  dark: githubDarkTheme,\\n  darkSelector: '.dark',\\n})\\n\\nexport default function render(output: HTMLElement) {\\n  const style = document.createElement('style')\\n  style.textContent = `${themeCss}\\nbody { margin: 0; padding: 24px; font-family: ui-sans-serif, system-ui; }\\npre.th-code { margin: 0; border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 16%, transparent); border-radius: 12px; }\\ncode { font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Consolas, monospace; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.65; }\\n.is-focused { background: color-mix(in srgb, #8250df 14%, transparent); }\\n.is-error { text-decoration: underline wavy var(--notebook-error); text-underline-offset: 3px; }\\n.hint { margin: 12px 4px 0; color: color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 70%, transparent); font-size: 13px; }`\\n\\n  document.head.append(style)\\n  output.innerHTML = `${result.html}<p class=\\\"hint\\\">Hover the underlined identifier to read its diagnostic.</p>`\\n\\n  const diagnostic = output.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.is-error')\\n  if (diagnostic) diagnostic.title = diagnostic.dataset.message ?? ''\\n}\"}}"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import { createHighlighter } from '@tanstack/highlight/core'\nimport { ts } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/ts'\nimport { createThemeCss } from '@tanstack/highlight/theme'\nimport { githubDarkTheme } from '@tanstack/highlight/themes/github-dark'\nimport { githubLightTheme } from '@tanstack/highlight/themes/github-light'\n\nconst source = [\n  'type User = { name: string }',\n  'const user = missingUser',\n  'console.log(user.name)',\n].join('\\n')\nconst identifier = 'missingUser'\nconst start = source.indexOf(identifier)\n\nconst highlighter = createHighlighter({ languages: [ts] })\nconst result = highlighter.highlight(source, {\n  lang: 'ts',\n  lineNumbers: true,\n  decorations: [\n    { lines: 3, className: 'is-focused' },\n    {\n      range: [start, start + identifier.length],\n      className: 'is-error',\n      data: { message: 'Unknown identifier' },\n    },\n  ],\n})\n\nconst themeCss = createThemeCss({\n  light: githubLightTheme,\n  dark: githubDarkTheme,\n  darkSelector: '.dark',\n})\n\nexport default function render(output: HTMLElement) {\n  const style = document.createElement('style')\n  style.textContent = `${themeCss}\nbody { margin: 0; padding: 24px; font-family: ui-sans-serif, system-ui; }\npre.th-code { margin: 0; border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 16%, transparent); border-radius: 12px; }\ncode { font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Consolas, monospace; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.65; }\n.is-focused { background: color-mix(in srgb, #8250df 14%, transparent); }\n.is-error { text-decoration: underline wavy var(--notebook-error); text-underline-offset: 3px; }\n.hint { margin: 12px 4px 0; color: color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 70%, transparent); font-size: 13px; }`\n\n  document.head.append(style)\n  output.innerHTML = `${result.html}<p class=\"hint\">Hover the underlined identifier to read its diagnostic.</p>`\n\n  const diagnostic = output.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.is-error')\n  if (diagnostic) diagnostic.title = diagnostic.dataset.message ?? ''\n}","lang":"ts","meta":"group=highlight-annotations file=/src/main.ts entry env=client","title":"/src/main.ts","file":"/src/main.ts"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"fence-annotations","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Fence annotations"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Markdown helpers recognize common metadata:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"```tsx title=\"App.tsx\" {2,4-6} ins={8} del={9} error={11} lineNumbers\n```","lang":"md"},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Syntax"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Class"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{2,4-6}"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"th-line--highlighted"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"highlight={2}"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"th-line--highlighted"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ins={2}"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"th-line--inserted"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"del={2}"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"th-line--deleted"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"focus={2}"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"th-line--focused"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"error={2}"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"th-line--error"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"warning={2}"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"th-line--warning"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"title"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"filename"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"file"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"name"},{"type":"text","value":" are accepted title keys. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"lineNumbers"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"showLineNumbers"},{"type":"text","value":" enable numbers."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"inline-diff-notation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Inline diff notation"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Markdown adapters also recognize the diff notation used by Shiki:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"- const oldValue = true // [!code --]\n+ const newValue = true // [!code ++]","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The directives are removed before tokenization and copying. Their lines receive "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"th-line--deleted"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"th-line--inserted"},{"type":"text","value":", respectively. JavaScript-style line and block comments, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"#"},{"type":"text","value":" line comments, and HTML comments are supported."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"styling","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Styling"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Annotation classes are intentionally unstyled:"}]},{"type":"code","value":".th-line--highlighted { background: rgb(9 105 218 / 10%); }\n.th-line--inserted { background: rgb(26 127 55 / 12%); }\n.th-line--deleted { background: rgb(207 34 46 / 12%); }\n.th-line--error { text-decoration: underline wavy #cf222e; }\n.th-line--focused { opacity: 1; }\n.th-code:has(.th-line--focused) .th-line:not(.th-line--focused) { opacity: 0.55; }","lang":"css"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"data"},{"type":"text","value":" for tooltips, diagnostics, IDs, or application hooks. Values are stringified and escaped."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"annotations","text":"Annotations","level":1},{"id":"line-decorations","text":"Line decorations","level":2},{"id":"character-range-decorations","text":"Character-range decorations","level":2},{"id":"line-numbers","text":"Line numbers","level":2},{"id":"try-annotations","text":"Try annotations","level":2},{"id":"fence-annotations","text":"Fence annotations","level":2},{"id":"inline-diff-notation","text":"Inline diff notation","level":2},{"id":"styling","text":"Styling","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n# Annotations\n\nAnnotations add application classes and data to lines or exact source ranges without changing the token stream.\n\n## Line decorations\n\nLine numbers are one-based:\n\n```ts\nconst result = highlighter.highlight(code, {\n  lang: 'ts',\n  decorations: [\n    { lines: 2, className: 'is-focused' },\n    { lines: [4, 6], className: 'is-highlighted' },\n  ],\n})\n```\n\n`lines: [4, 6]` includes lines 4, 5, and 6.\n\nLine decorations activate `th-line` wrappers even when `lineNumbers` is false.\n\n## Character-range decorations\n\nCharacter ranges are zero-based, end-exclusive UTF-16 offsets, matching `String.prototype.slice()`:\n\n```ts\nconst code = `const answer = unknownValue`\nconst start = code.indexOf('unknownValue')\n\nconst result = highlighter.highlight(code, {\n  lang: 'ts',\n  decorations: [\n    {\n      range: [start, start + 'unknownValue'.length],\n      className: 'is-error',\n      data: { message: 'Unknown identifier', severity: 2 },\n    },\n  ],\n})\n```\n\nThe renderer splits token boundaries as needed and wraps the selected text with `th-decoration` plus your classes. Overlapping decorations remain valid nested HTML.\n\n## Line numbers\n\n```ts\nhighlighter.highlight(code, {\n  lang: 'ts',\n  lineNumbers: true,\n})\n```\n\nThis adds `th-code--line-numbers`, line wrappers, and `data-line`. Base theme CSS renders the number with `::before`.\n\n## Try annotations\n\nThe rendered block combines line numbers, a focused line, and an exact character-range diagnostic.\n\n```ts group=highlight-annotations file=/src/main.ts entry env=client\nimport { createHighlighter } from '@tanstack/highlight/core'\nimport { ts } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/ts'\nimport { createThemeCss } from '@tanstack/highlight/theme'\nimport { githubDarkTheme } from '@tanstack/highlight/themes/github-dark'\nimport { githubLightTheme } from '@tanstack/highlight/themes/github-light'\n\nconst source = [\n  'type User = { name: string }',\n  'const user = missingUser',\n  'console.log(user.name)',\n].join('\\n')\nconst identifier = 'missingUser'\nconst start = source.indexOf(identifier)\n\nconst highlighter = createHighlighter({ languages: [ts] })\nconst result = highlighter.highlight(source, {\n  lang: 'ts',\n  lineNumbers: true,\n  decorations: [\n    { lines: 3, className: 'is-focused' },\n    {\n      range: [start, start + identifier.length],\n      className: 'is-error',\n      data: { message: 'Unknown identifier' },\n    },\n  ],\n})\n\nconst themeCss = createThemeCss({\n  light: githubLightTheme,\n  dark: githubDarkTheme,\n  darkSelector: '.dark',\n})\n\nexport default function render(output: HTMLElement) {\n  const style = document.createElement('style')\n  style.textContent = `${themeCss}\nbody { margin: 0; padding: 24px; font-family: ui-sans-serif, system-ui; }\npre.th-code { margin: 0; border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 16%, transparent); border-radius: 12px; }\ncode { font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Consolas, monospace; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.65; }\n.is-focused { background: color-mix(in srgb, #8250df 14%, transparent); }\n.is-error { text-decoration: underline wavy var(--notebook-error); text-underline-offset: 3px; }\n.hint { margin: 12px 4px 0; color: color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 70%, transparent); font-size: 13px; }`\n\n  document.head.append(style)\n  output.innerHTML = `${result.html}<p class=\"hint\">Hover the underlined identifier to read its diagnostic.</p>`\n\n  const diagnostic = output.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.is-error')\n  if (diagnostic) diagnostic.title = diagnostic.dataset.message ?? ''\n}\n```\n\n## Fence annotations\n\nThe Markdown helpers recognize common metadata:\n\n````md\n```tsx title=\"App.tsx\" {2,4-6} ins={8} del={9} error={11} lineNumbers\n```\n````\n\n| Syntax | Class |\n| --- | --- |\n| `{2,4-6}` | `th-line--highlighted` |\n| `highlight={2}` | `th-line--highlighted` |\n| `ins={2}` | `th-line--inserted` |\n| `del={2}` | `th-line--deleted` |\n| `focus={2}` | `th-line--focused` |\n| `error={2}` | `th-line--error` |\n| `warning={2}` | `th-line--warning` |\n\n`title`, `filename`, `file`, and `name` are accepted title keys. `lineNumbers` and `showLineNumbers` enable numbers.\n\n## Inline diff notation\n\nMarkdown adapters also recognize the diff notation used by Shiki:\n\n```ts\n- const oldValue = true // [!code --]\n+ const newValue = true // [!code ++]\n```\n\nThe directives are removed before tokenization and copying. Their lines receive `th-line--deleted` and `th-line--inserted`, respectively. JavaScript-style line and block comments, `#` line comments, and HTML comments are supported.\n\n## Styling\n\nAnnotation classes are intentionally unstyled:\n\n```css\n.th-line--highlighted { background: rgb(9 105 218 / 10%); }\n.th-line--inserted { background: rgb(26 127 55 / 12%); }\n.th-line--deleted { background: rgb(207 34 46 / 12%); }\n.th-line--error { text-decoration: underline wavy #cf222e; }\n.th-line--focused { opacity: 1; }\n.th-code:has(.th-line--focused) .th-line:not(.th-line--focused) { opacity: 0.55; }\n```\n\nUse `data` for tooltips, diagnostics, IDs, or application hooks. Values are stringified and escaped.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Annotations\n---\n\n# Annotations\n\nAnnotations add application classes and data to lines or exact source ranges without changing the token stream.\n\n## Line decorations\n\nLine numbers are one-based:\n\n```ts\nconst result = highlighter.highlight(code, {\n  lang: 'ts',\n  decorations: [\n    { lines: 2, className: 'is-focused' },\n    { lines: [4, 6], className: 'is-highlighted' },\n  ],\n})\n```\n\n`lines: [4, 6]` includes lines 4, 5, and 6.\n\nLine decorations activate `th-line` wrappers even when `lineNumbers` is false.\n\n## Character-range decorations\n\nCharacter ranges are zero-based, end-exclusive UTF-16 offsets, matching `String.prototype.slice()`:\n\n```ts\nconst code = `const answer = unknownValue`\nconst start = code.indexOf('unknownValue')\n\nconst result = highlighter.highlight(code, {\n  lang: 'ts',\n  decorations: [\n    {\n      range: [start, start + 'unknownValue'.length],\n      className: 'is-error',\n      data: { message: 'Unknown identifier', severity: 2 },\n    },\n  ],\n})\n```\n\nThe renderer splits token boundaries as needed and wraps the selected text with `th-decoration` plus your classes. Overlapping decorations remain valid nested HTML.\n\n## Line numbers\n\n```ts\nhighlighter.highlight(code, {\n  lang: 'ts',\n  lineNumbers: true,\n})\n```\n\nThis adds `th-code--line-numbers`, line wrappers, and `data-line`. Base theme CSS renders the number with `::before`.\n\n## Try annotations\n\nThe rendered block combines line numbers, a focused line, and an exact character-range diagnostic.\n\n```ts group=highlight-annotations file=/src/main.ts entry env=client\nimport { createHighlighter } from '@tanstack/highlight/core'\nimport { ts } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/ts'\nimport { createThemeCss } from '@tanstack/highlight/theme'\nimport { githubDarkTheme } from '@tanstack/highlight/themes/github-dark'\nimport { githubLightTheme } from '@tanstack/highlight/themes/github-light'\n\nconst source = [\n  'type User = { name: string }',\n  'const user = missingUser',\n  'console.log(user.name)',\n].join('\\n')\nconst identifier = 'missingUser'\nconst start = source.indexOf(identifier)\n\nconst highlighter = createHighlighter({ languages: [ts] })\nconst result = highlighter.highlight(source, {\n  lang: 'ts',\n  lineNumbers: true,\n  decorations: [\n    { lines: 3, className: 'is-focused' },\n    {\n      range: [start, start + identifier.length],\n      className: 'is-error',\n      data: { message: 'Unknown identifier' },\n    },\n  ],\n})\n\nconst themeCss = createThemeCss({\n  light: githubLightTheme,\n  dark: githubDarkTheme,\n  darkSelector: '.dark',\n})\n\nexport default function render(output: HTMLElement) {\n  const style = document.createElement('style')\n  style.textContent = `${themeCss}\nbody { margin: 0; padding: 24px; font-family: ui-sans-serif, system-ui; }\npre.th-code { margin: 0; border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 16%, transparent); border-radius: 12px; }\ncode { font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Consolas, monospace; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.65; }\n.is-focused { background: color-mix(in srgb, #8250df 14%, transparent); }\n.is-error { text-decoration: underline wavy var(--notebook-error); text-underline-offset: 3px; }\n.hint { margin: 12px 4px 0; color: color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 70%, transparent); font-size: 13px; }`\n\n  document.head.append(style)\n  output.innerHTML = `${result.html}<p class=\"hint\">Hover the underlined identifier to read its diagnostic.</p>`\n\n  const diagnostic = output.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.is-error')\n  if (diagnostic) diagnostic.title = diagnostic.dataset.message ?? ''\n}\n```\n\n## Fence annotations\n\nThe Markdown helpers recognize common metadata:\n\n````md\n```tsx title=\"App.tsx\" {2,4-6} ins={8} del={9} error={11} lineNumbers\n```\n````\n\n| Syntax | Class |\n| --- | --- |\n| `{2,4-6}` | `th-line--highlighted` |\n| `highlight={2}` | `th-line--highlighted` |\n| `ins={2}` | `th-line--inserted` |\n| `del={2}` | `th-line--deleted` |\n| `focus={2}` | `th-line--focused` |\n| `error={2}` | `th-line--error` |\n| `warning={2}` | `th-line--warning` |\n\n`title`, `filename`, `file`, and `name` are accepted title keys. `lineNumbers` and `showLineNumbers` enable numbers.\n\n## Inline diff notation\n\nMarkdown adapters also recognize the diff notation used by Shiki:\n\n```ts\n- const oldValue = true // [!code --]\n+ const newValue = true // [!code ++]\n```\n\nThe directives are removed before tokenization and copying. Their lines receive `th-line--deleted` and `th-line--inserted`, respectively. JavaScript-style line and block comments, `#` line comments, and HTML comments are supported.\n\n## Styling\n\nAnnotation classes are intentionally unstyled:\n\n```css\n.th-line--highlighted { background: rgb(9 105 218 / 10%); }\n.th-line--inserted { background: rgb(26 127 55 / 12%); }\n.th-line--deleted { background: rgb(207 34 46 / 12%); }\n.th-line--error { text-decoration: underline wavy #cf222e; }\n.th-line--focused { opacity: 1; }\n.th-code:has(.th-line--focused) .th-line:not(.th-line--focused) { opacity: 0.55; }\n```\n\nUse `data` for tooltips, diagnostics, IDs, or application hooks. Values are stringified and escaped.\n"}
